cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this work, please cite it as below.
title: "What actually inflates a forecasting score, the split, or the horizon?"
abstract: "Time-series evaluation protocol, measured: the horizon inflates a forecasting score 10x more than the train/test split, and refitting daily for a month is worth 0.3%. Both premises this project was built on, refuted."
type: software
